---
description: Styling and accessibility rules
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Styling

- Use styled-components and MUI components; avoid inline styles.
- Prefer design tokens over magic numbers. Centralize spacing, colors, and typography via theme.
- Favor margin-bottom for vertical rhythm; avoid margin-top except for exceptions.

Positioning

- Avoid `position: absolute` except for decorative or non-essential elements. Provide a11y labels if used.

Accessibility

- Ensure interactive elements have proper roles, labels, and focus states.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion and color-contrast guidelines when feasible.
